  body: "# Attendance Allowance care needs in the source\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe AA introduction describes
    needs for attention, supervision or watching over and identifies a single component with higher and lower rates.\n\
    \n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe source separately requires age, residence/presence/competency and disability
    conditions. It does not establish entitlement from age, a diagnosis or a care need alone. The printed age paragraph
    on page 5 lacks the expected 61013 number in this extraction; it is not silently invented.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 61001, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/695ba618295a95414df21af4/dmg-ch-61.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 61002, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/695ba618295a95414df21af4/dmg-ch-61.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 61012, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/695ba618295a95414df21af4/dmg-ch-61.pdf#page=4).\n\
    \n## Additional context\n\n- [Context: chapter 61, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/695ba618295a95414df21af4/dmg-ch-61.pdf#page=5).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch61`:
    PDF `884dc79907770bd9e178fe4122c0b7d404697f4ccc882b067e9220b34a0f002a`; extracted pages `23b4405d725de2fde124df29a8c753b9fcb7530405c83d588bd321e1e83226cc`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.783276Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/695ba618295a95414df21af4/dmg-ch-61.pdf#page=3
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dla-component-distinction
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter contrasts AA’s one component with DLA’s separate care and mobility components.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch61/0003
      quote: "61002 There is only one AA component made with two rates which are\n\n\n1. the higher rate and\n\n\
        \n2. the lower rate.\n\n\nSeverely disabled people may be entitled to either of these rates. The rate depends
        on the level of\n\nattention, supervision or watching over a person needs1.\n\n\n                      \
        \                                                               1 SS CB Act 92, s 64"
      locator: DMG 61002
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch61/0004
      quote: "61009 DLA is made up of two components. These are\n\n\n1. the care component and\n\n\n2. the mobility
        component.\n\n\nA disabled person may be entitled to one or both components. See guidance in DMG 61603 for
        claims\nwith evidence of one component only."
      locator: DMG 61009
  - target: term/aa-dla-medical-advice
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter treats medical advice as evidence assisting the DM, not as a claim determination.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch61/0007
      quote: "61024 If the DM has difficulty in interpreting the medical evidence the case may be referred to Medical\n\
        Services for advice. In the event of an appeal, the advice should be put before the tribunal for comment.\n\
        DMs should consider the guidance in DMG Chapter 03 when giving consideration to a medical opinion.\nWhere
        the Medical Services advice conflicts with the claimed needs, the DM should consider whether\nfurther evidence
        needs to be obtained.\n\n\nNote: Medical Services have no authority to determine claims and cannot advise
        directly on whether a\nperson satisfies one of the disability tests."
      locator: DMG 61024
